1. Printable parts

The seven printable STLs this repository analyses are generated by build.py in
the owner's separate design directory (microduck-braccio-unoq). They are flat
plates with the owner's servo cradles, horn blanks and board deck. For the
silhouette of each plate the script started from the convex outline, in one
projection, of one of 15 meshes from a pack named "Microduck robot duck
structural parts (simulation model export, 15 pieces)" (the name is in
Chinese). The pack holds only STL files, with no licence, readme or author;
its part names match the Microduck by Pollen Robotics
(https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl).

None of those meshes, and nothing of their surfaces, joints or mechanisms, is
in this repository or in the printable parts. The owner compared the result
with the original and judged it a different design; this note records where
the outlines came from. The generated printable STLs are committed in stl/
with a manifest; scripts/fetch_stls.py copies them from the local design
directory when they are regenerated. The 15 source meshes are not in this
repository.

Nothing was copied from microduck_rl. Its joint names and ranges were read for
comparison only.

2. unoq-braccio-sketchbot (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Edge Impulse Sketchbot
   contributors), the owner's repository this one follows

  - app_lab/microduck_agent/sketch/BraccioPulse.hpp is copied unchanged.
