7. Microduck-look biped (stl/microduck-look/, microduck/look/, docs/microduck-look.md)

Unlike the plates of section 1, the parts in stl/microduck-look/ reproduce
the shells of the Microduck by Pollen Robotics
(https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl): body halves, thigh covers,
feet, head shells, face plate, eye ring and beak, taken from the part pack
described in section 1, which was exported from their simulation model. They
are an adaptation of that model. Pollen Robotics' repository states: "3D model
files are licensed under Creative Commons BY-SA-NC". It names no version;
version 4.0 is used here.

The STL files in stl/microduck-look/ (the comb feet left_foot_comb.stl and
right_foot_comb.stl included, which are made from the two feet),
stl/microduck-look/parameters.json and comb_feet.json, the pictures in
stl/microduck-look/images/ and stl/thumbs/microduck-look/, the card picture
docs/images/build-look.png and the shapes in robot/microduck-look/ are
therefore licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode),
not under the MIT licence.

  Credit: Adapted from the Microduck by Pollen Robotics,
  https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl

  Changes: scaled by 1.25; re-split into printable solids and simplified;
  the servo mounts replaced by cradles and horn plates for TinkerKit Braccio
  servos and 9 g servos, with three joint axes moved; covers, feet and head
  shell cut back where the new parts turn; the soles widened towards the
  centre line; a trunk frame with a back plate for two boards and a camera
  seat behind the eye added; for the comb feet, part of that web cut away and
  fingers added that cross the centre line. The full list is in
  stl/microduck-look/LICENSE.

The 15 source meshes are not in this repository. The code under
microduck/look/ and scripts/run_look.py is MIT. "Microduck" is the name of
Pollen Robotics' robot and is used only to say what the parts were adapted
from; this project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Pollen Robotics,
who sell the original.

Sources of the component data for this build are listed in
config/microduck-look/build.json.
